  "Question": "A product costs 80 yuan and has a marked price of 120 yuan. The store sells it at \\(x\\) tenths of the marked price. To achieve a profit rate of at least \\(20\\%\\), what is the minimum number of tenths? (Enter the minimum value of \\(x\\).)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The selling price is \\(120\\times x/10\\). A profit rate of at least \\(20\\%\\) means the selling price must be \\(\\geq80\\times1.2=96\\), so \\(12x\\geq96\\), giving \\(x\\geq8\\). Thus, the minimum selling price is 8 tenths of the marked price.",
